@startuml

title US11 - Register Parameter\nDomain Model (DM)

skinparam backgroundColor #FFFFFF
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam classAttributeIconSize 0
skinparam classBorderColor #2563EB
skinparam classBackgroundColor #EFF6FF
skinparam ArrowColor #475569
skinparam NoteBackgroundColor #FFF9E6
skinparam linetype ortho

hide methods
hide circle

' =====================================================
' Domain concepts
' =====================================================

class Administrator

class Parameter {
    code
    name
    description
    metric
    metricType
}

class ReferenceRange {
    minimum
    maximum
}

class TestType {
    internalCode
    nhsCode
    collectionMethodDescription
}

class TestTypeParameter

' =====================================================
' Domain associations
' =====================================================

Administrator "0..*" -- "0..*" Parameter : manages >

Parameter "1" -- "0..1" ReferenceRange : has >

TestType "1" -- "1..*" TestTypeParameter : defines >

TestTypeParameter "0..*" -- "1" Parameter : identifies >

' =====================================================
' Business rules
' =====================================================

note right of Parameter
AC11-1

Each parameter has a unique
code containing exactly five
alphanumeric characters.

AC11-2

Reference values are applicable
only to numeric metrics.

For Numeric, both bounds
are mandatory.
end note

note bottom of ReferenceRange
Numeric parameter:
exactly one reference range,
with both bounds mandatory.

Qualitative parameter:
no reference range.

minimum <= maximum.
end note

note bottom of TestTypeParameter
Associates test types
with their parameters.

This concept already exists
in the global Domain Model.
end note

note top of Parameter
Metric classification:

Numeric
Qualitative

Represented in the CD
by the MetricType enumeration.
end note

@enduml